{"id": "array-2026-09-11-009", "date": "2026-09-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["array"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Array Technologies triples its U.S. manufacturing footprint", "content": "<p>The Albuquerque solar tracker manufacturing facility will employ about 300 people and enable it to bring production in house rather than sourcing components from other suppliers.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/array-technologies-triples-its-u-s-manufacturing-footprint/\">Array Technologies triples its U.S. manufacturing footprint</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/array-technologies-triples-its-u-s-manufacturing-footprint/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-11-010", "date": "2026-09-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Solarize Africa: The case of Madagascar", "content": "<p>Madagascar’s diesel-dependent power system faces high costs and chronic blackouts, making solar PV and battery storage an increasingly attractive route to reliable, affordable electrification. Five solar-diesel hybrid projects demonstrate that PV can significantly reduce fuel consumption and electricity prices, offering a scalable model for Madagascar and wider sub-Saharan Africa.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/solarize-africa-the-case-of-madagascar/\">Solarize", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/solarize-africa-the-case-of-madagascar/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-11-011", "date": "2026-09-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "‘I make a point of thanking people for asking critical questions and disagreeing openly’", "content": "<p>This week, Women in Solar+ Europe gives voice to Hanna König, Head of Division Project Execution, at Germany's Enertrag SE. She says the most important element of an inclusive organisational culture is ensuring that everyone feels safe to contribute ideas and opinions, particularly when they disagree with the majority or with people in more senior positions. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/i-make-a-point-of-thanking-people-for-asking-critical-questions-and-dis", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/i-make-a-point-of-thanking-people-for-asking-critical-questions-and-disagreeing-openly/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-11-012", "date": "2026-09-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["[否定]loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Sunny north and cloudy south as Super El Niño defines South American winter", "content": "<p>In a new weekly update for <b>pv magazine</b>, Solcast, a DNV company, reports that Super El Niño drove a sharp north–south irradiance divide across South America in winter 2026, with sunnier conditions in the north and persistent cloud reducing solar irradiance across much of the south. Two rare August snowstorms in Chile’s Atacama Desert also caused likely snow-related losses for solar PV assets, alongside severe rainfall, flooding, and mudslides.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-mag", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/sunny-north-and-cloudy-south-as-super-el-nino-defines-south-american-winter/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-11-013", "date": "2026-09-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South Korea forecast to add 3.5 GW of solar in 2026", "content": "<p>The Export–Import Bank of Korea says the country is on track to add more this solar this year than last year, as the Korean government works on developing a distributed power grid that facilitates greater integration of distributed energy resources.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/south-korea-forecast-to-add-3-5-gw-of-solar-in-2026/\">South Korea forecast to add 3.5 GW of solar in 2026</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Globa", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/south-korea-forecast-to-add-3-5-gw-of-solar-in-2026/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "gcl-2026-09-11-014", "date": "2026-09-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["gcl", "tongwei", "jinko", "longi"], "customers": ["longi"], "suppliers": ["gcl", "tongwei"]}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["expand", "improve", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.7, "reasons": ["多公司提及"]}, "title": "Chinese PV Industry Brief: Tongwei clears antitrust hurdle for acquisition of polysilicon competitor Qinghai Lihao", "content": "<p>In other news, Longi said its operating conditions are expected to improve after a CNY 3.68 billion ($542 million) first-half loss, while GCL SI and Ant Digital Technologies agreed to develop an AI-enabled carbon-management platform. JinkoSolar, meanwhile, proposed renaming its overseas parent Jinko Holdings Limited as it expands beyond solar manufacturing into strategic investments.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/tongwei-clears-antitrust-hurdle-for-acquisitio", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/tongwei-clears-antitrust-hurdle-for-acquisition-of-polysilicon-competitor-qinghai-lihao/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-11-015", "date": "2026-09-11", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The Hydrogen Stream: AEM electrolysis could deliver hydrogen at $3.27/kg, say Repsol, P2HP", "content": "<p>Power to Hydrogen (P2H2) and Repsol completed a 1,250-hour pilot of P2H2’s hybrid AEM electrolyzer technology, demonstrating operation at 40% to 100% load, pressures up to 30 bar and hydrogen purity of up to 99.9%. P2H2 projects an LCOH of €3.86 ($4.47)/kg, potentially falling to €2.82/kg under optimized renewable energy conditions, and the companies are considering a 500 kW-to-MW-scale demonstration.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/the-hydrogen-stream-aem-elec", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/11/the-hydrogen-stream-aem-electrolysis-could-deliver-hydrogen-at-3-27-kg-say-repsol-p2hp/", "type": "rss"}]}
